        "text": "For a reversible adiabatic process, \\(q=0\\).\n\nFor a monoatomic ideal gas:\n\\[\nC_V=\\frac{3}{2}R,\\qquad C_P=\\frac{5}{2}R,\\qquad \\gamma=\\frac{5}{3}\n\\]\n\nAdiabatic relation:\n\\[\nT_2=T_1\\left(\\frac{V_1}{V_2}\\right)^{\\gamma-1}\n\\]\n\\[\nT_1=45^\\circ C=318.15\\text{ K}\n\\]\n\\[\nT_2=318.15\\left(\\frac{75}{20}\\right)^{2/3}\\approx 767.8\\text{ K}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\Delta T\\approx 449.7\\text{ K}\n\\]\n\nInternal energy change:\n\\[\n\\Delta E=nC_V\\Delta T=2\\left(\\frac{3}{2}R\\right)(449.7)\\approx 11.21\\text{ kJ}\n\\]\n\nEnthalpy change:\n\\[\n\\Delta H=nC_P\\Delta T=2\\left(\\frac{5}{2}R\\right)(449.7)\\approx 18.68\\text{ kJ}\n\\]\n\nThus:\n\\[\nq=0,\\quad \\Delta E=11.21\\text{ kJ},\\quad \\Delta H=18.68\\text{ kJ}\n\\]\n\nAnswer: E",
