        "expected": "A",
        "status": "passed",
        "got": "A",
        "text": "For laminar flow, use the Hagen–Poiseuille head loss:\n\n\\[\nh_f=\\frac{32\\mu V L}{\\rho g D^2}\n\\]\n\nGiven:\n\n\\[\nD=\\frac{1}{4}\\text{ in}=\\frac{0.25}{12}=0.020833\\text{ ft}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nL=16\\text{ ft}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\mu=0.679\\times10^{-3}\\text{ lbm/ft-s}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\rho \\approx 62.4\\text{ lbm/ft}^3\n\\]\n\nCritical Reynolds number:\n\n\\[\nRe_c=2500\n\\]\n\nSince the flow is at half the critical velocity,\n\n\\[\nRe=1250\n\\]\n\nKinematic viscosity:\n\n\\[\n\\nu=\\frac{\\mu}{\\rho}\n=\\frac{0.679\\times10^{-3}}{62.4}\n=1.088\\times10^{-5}\\text{ ft}^2/\\text{s}\n\\]\n\nVelocity:\n\n\\[\nV=\\frac{Re\\,\\nu}{D}\n=\\frac{1250(1.088\\times10^{-5})}{0.020833}\n=0.653\\text{ ft/s}\n\\]\n\nHead loss:\n\n\\[\nh_f=\\frac{32\\nu V L}{gD^2}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nh_f=\\frac{32(1.088\\times10^{-5})(0.653)(16)}\n{32.2(0.020833)^2}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nh_f=0.260\\text{ ft}\n\\]\n\nConvert to inches:\n\n\\[\n0.260(12)=3.12\\text{ in}\n\\]\n\nAnswer: A",
